## Worksheet

**F1 Core loop** — Game class = single state object; mulberry32 seeds all RNG use (map, colonists, events, storms); endTurn() runs fixed order (event→production→consumption→colonist update→storm→trade→win/loss). Score 2.

**F2 Map** — generateMap() builds 8x8 from seeded rng; buildBuilding() checks tile.terrain vs building.terrain; getAdjacencyBonuses() returns +15/+20%, stored as adjBonus, read in runProduction(). Score 2.

**F3 Economy** — power(reactor)→metal(forge/smelter, needs power)→parts(partsFab, needs metal+power) chain; storageCaps enforced with overflow logged in runProduction(). Input consumption is a flat -1/turn (shallow) but chain and caps are real. Score 2.

**F4 Population** — colonists have skill/fatigue/morale/job/assigned; skill read via skillSum in runProduction(), but fatigue is only read by updateColonistStates() (affects morale), never by production code. Score 1.

**F5 Needs** — runConsumption() computes food/water deficit, drops colonist.morale by 5; but morale is never read anywhere in runProduction() so it never changes output. Score 1.

**F6 Research** — 12 RESEARCH_NODES defined, but "Research" button is `onclick="alert('TODO: Research mechanics')"` — no function ever sets research[id].done=true or applies node.effect (explicit `// TODO: Apply research bonuses`). Score 0.

**F7 Events** — 15 events, fireEvent() called from endTurn() and resolveEvent() mutates state for several outcomes, but selection is uniform (`EVENTS[Math.floor(rng()*EVENTS.length)]`, weight field unused), eventCooldown is set but never checked, and only 1 event (desertion) has both choice branches produce distinct real mutations — rest are TODO stubs. Score 1.

**F8 Trade** — caravan open/close toggled by tradeCaravanTurns, caravanGoods rendered, but "Buy" button is `onclick="alert('TODO: Buy/sell mechanics')"` — no buy or sell function exists. Score 0.

**F9 Hazard** — triggerStorm() called from endTurn(), severity scales with turn, health penalty read in runProduction(), shield buildings reduce damage; but "Repair" button is `alert('TODO: Repair/dismantle mechanics')` — no repair function anywhere, damage is permanent. Score 1.

**F10 Save/load** — getSaveState()/loadFromState() exist and are used by the self-test round-trip, but no textarea or export/import UI exists anywhere in the HTML for the player. Score 0.

**F11 End conditions** — endTurn() checks colonists.length===0 (loss) and turn>=60 && pop>=12 (win), both reachable; showEndScreen() computes score from colonists/research/resources/turn and renders modal. Score 2.

**F12 UI** — switchTab() wired to all tab buttons; addLog() stores turn, renderLog() shows "T{turn}:"; keydown listener wires Space and 1-5; @media query adapts sidebar/tile size; but .tooltip CSS class is never instantiated anywhere in JS. Score 1.

**F13 Dev panel** — runTests() has 15 real invariant checks (caps, ranges, prereqs, save/load roundtrip, PRNG determinism); runBenchmark() runs a headless 200-turn loop with a greedy policy and prints hashState() output. Score 2.

**G1** — research effects never applied (F6=0), runProduction has literal `// TODO: Apply research bonuses from unlocked techs`. Score 0.

**G2** — runConsumption() writes deficit→morale-=5 (real state change), but runProduction() never reads colonist.morale, so labor output is unaffected. Score 1.

**G3** — triggerStorm() damages building.health; runProduction() scales output by health/maxHealth (real link); shield building mitigates damage; but no repair function exists anywhere, so "repair cost"/"recovery" links are absent. Score 2.

**G4** — caravanGoods prices in renderTrade() are hardcoded literals (2,3,8,5,15), never derived from this.resources or a drifting supply variable. Score 0.

**G5** — resolveEvent() case 'desertion' has both choices (popLoss splice, moraleLoss on all colonists) durably mutate state differently; most other choice events (outbreak, equipment, mostly mutation/outsiders/accident) have at least one branch reduced to `// TODO: Implement remaining outcomes` log-only stub. Score 2.

